of times slower, as the introduction explains. The same holds for .NET: a Debug build
normally tells the JIT compiler not to optimize, so that a debugger can inspect every local
variable. [[Optimize]] set unconditionally undoes that for this one assembly. Debugging the core
becomes a little harder, and the app stays usable in Debug.

