@ \subsection{Filter values}

A Swift enumeration with associated values has no direct C\# equivalent. The idiom that comes
closest is an abstract record with one nested sealed record per case. Records provide the value
equality that [[Equatable]] gave, including for the parameters, and a [[switch]] on the type with
positional patterns takes the place of [[case .gaussianBlur(let r)]]. Parameterless cases like
[[Median]] are records without fields: any two instances compare equal. The hierarchy is open as
far as the compiler knows, so each switch needs a discard arm that is never reached.

<<Win Filters: the [[FilterKind]] records>>=
