\section{The spectrum}\label{sec:win-spectrum}

The spectrum keeps everything of Chapter~\ref{ch:analysis} that defines the numbers on the
screen: the zero padding to a power of two, the optional mean removal, the symmetric Hann window,
the single-sided amplitudes divided by the window sum, and the two frequency axes. What changes is
the transform underneath. vDSP isn't available, and rather than take a dependency for one
function, the port carries its own FFT.

